# The Public programme documentation packages ship SHA256SUMS.txt, and their
# integrity evidence is byte-exact: reports/PUBLIC_DOCS_LOADED_REPORT.md records
# 13/13 files verifying OK, and that verification is what authorises the v0.2
# package as the controlling implementation input.
#
# PCA_PUBLIC_CLAIM_REGISTER.csv (v0.1 and v0.2) is authored with CRLF line
# endings. The repository root .gitattributes sets `* text=auto eol=lf`, which
# would normalise it to LF on checkout -- changing its bytes, and therefore its
# SHA256, so a fresh clone would FAIL `sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS.txt`. Measured,
# not assumed: the manifest expects 72b7390108cc338b..., the LF-normalised file
# hashes to 29e4bc9384650e3c...
#
# `-text` disables all line-ending conversion for these files so the packages
# stay verifiable exactly as the owner issued them. This is a directory-local
# override deliberately scoped to docs/public/ -- it changes nothing elsewhere
# in the repository and touches no shared configuration file.
#
# It applies to the checksummed packages only. Reports and addenda in this
# directory are ordinary markdown and keep the repository-wide LF rule.
PCA_Public_Programme_Documentation_Package_v0.1/** -text
PCA_Public_Programme_Documentation_Package_v0.2/** -text

# The independent Arabic reviewer package is EVIDENCE. It is stored exactly as
# supplied, CRLF included, so its checksums stay verifiable -- the same reason
# the frozen v0.2 package above is protected. LF normalisation silently changes
# the bytes of a file whose whole value is being unchanged.
reports/PCA_Release_A_Arabic_Native_Review_Package/** -text
